	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/video_settings/frame_rate/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Shows each frame at a refresh of the display: even motion that never tears. With Low Latency it adds almost no input lag. It is on in the Steam Deck's Game Mode."/>
		<string text="For a G-SYNC or FreeSync display: VSync on and the frame rate held just under the refresh rate, so each frame shows as soon as it is ready, without tearing. Auto turns it on where the system says VRR is on."/>
		<string text="Frames a second kept under the refresh rate, so the game stays in the screen's VRR range and never falls back to VSync. Lower is closer to the most frames; higher is safer on a screen with a narrow range.|Used while Variable Refresh is on."/>
		<string text="The most frames drawn a second with VSync off. Auto is twice the display's refresh rate. More feels smoother and uses more power; None draws as fast as it can.|Click the number (or press A) to type 10 to 1000."/>
		<string text="With VSync on, starts each frame just in time for the refresh it is shown at, so a press reaches the screen sooner. Off starts each frame as soon as the one before is waiting. Auto is on."/>
	</strings>
